These are the scripts used for the paper ["A high throughput method for determining structural and sequence variations in Leishmania genomes at single-cell level"]().

# Description
1) `scDNA_functions_S3.R`: This contains the functions used for karyotyping. It defines a `scDNA` S3 object, which is basically a list of dataframes and matrices containing counts (cells X bins) as well as cells metadata and bins metadata. All results regarding karyotypying are stored in this object.
2) `generate_karyotyping_objects.R`: This script performs the karyotyping calculations using the functions from `scDNA_functions_S3.R`. It exports a list of scDNA objects, one for each sample, as `.rds` files.
3) `generate_cells_metadata.R`: This script takes the `.rds` files generated by `generate_karyotyping_objects.R` and exports a `.tsv` file containing all metadata for all cells. 
4) `install_ScisTree2.sh`: This is a small script that installs [ScisTree2](https://github.com/yufengwudcs/ScisTree2) using a conda environment. Was written for personal use.
5) `prepare_af_matrices_for_scistree2.R`: This `R` script takes the raw allele depth (ad) matrices generated by GATK, filter high count loci and split the matrices per strain so they can be used in `ScisTree2.py`.
6) `ScisTree2.py`: This script runs [ScisTree2](https://github.com/yufengwudcs/ScisTree2) to infer phylogenies between cells. 
7) `color_palettes.R`: Small `R` script that defines the color palletes used in the plots. is loaded by the `Figure X.R` scripts.
7) `Figure 1.R`: Generates the figure panel 1.
8) `Figure 2.R`: Generates the figure panel 2.
9) `Figure 3.R`: Generates the figure panel 3.
10) `Figure 4.R`: Generates the figure panel 4.
11) `Figure 5.R`: Generates the figure panel 5.
12) `generate_figures.sh`: This is a small script that runs all `Figure X.R` scripts and convert the figure panels (pdf) to png. 

